hoto":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-211812.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"latinbeauty","Id":211812,"Name":"latinbeauty","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":15009,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9e3ddc554bd4c19b0627fda4bbac57c5","RawContent":"Totally awesome!! I love the cover.","Attachments":[],"Id":467654,"PostDate":1222818322,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Totally awesome!! I love the cover.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"dwbride2011@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":5,"GroupName":"Banned","JoinDate":1222457820,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-211964.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"RosieM","Id":211964,"Name":"RosieM","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15009,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6520e5daa08db8e542c14515522ee3ba","RawContent":"awesome job we&#039;re doing ours also , wish us luck!!!!","Attachments":[],"Id":469306,"PostDate":1222926252,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                awesome job we're doing ours also , wish us luck!!!!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mimirdh1@aol.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1221292113,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-211702.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"rdhbride","Id":211702,"Name":"rdhbride","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15009,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2b77ff39ebe2dda34c55b051a032d754","RawContent":"&lt;div style=\"margin:20px; margin-top:5px; \"&gt; &lt;div class=\"smallfont\"&gt;Quote:&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\"&gt;  Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;Minde&lt;\/strong&gt; &lt;img class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"&gt;  &lt;div style=\"font-style:italic\"&gt;Here are all the pictures below...\n \n I used cover paper that you can get at Michaels. I found it a bit cheaper through a wholesale paper company but it is identical to the sparkly stuff they sell at Michaels. Laser printers will not work for metallic like paper! I tried 3! I printed that on a Lexmark 2500 all in one which feeds from the top and comes out the front. This is a must! anything that has to make a sharp turn won&#039;t work. I got that printer at Wal-Mart for about $50 I think. \n \n The inside sheets are HP brochure paper. Kinda slick and about 28 lb I think. No see through at all. Those I printed on a color laser printer but an inkjet would have done them too. \n \n I used Word to print the envelopes, again must be on a printer that feeds from the top and comes out the front or you will have marks on the envelope. I stamped the back and used a pretty stamp.\n \n Any other questions please ask. I cannot take credit for all of this as I learned and borrowed from others on here!\n \n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000917.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;\n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000918.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;\n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000919.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;\n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000921.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;\n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000922.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;\n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000923.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;\n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000924.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/td&gt; &lt;\/tr&gt; &lt;\/table&gt; &lt;\/div&gt;\n \n Question: The paper that is on the inside of the Passport - did the blue speck pattern print out as well? Or did you buy paper like that and then print on the paper?","Attachments":[],"Id":470646,"PostDate":1223017543,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <div  style=\"margin:20px\"> <div class=\"smallfont\">Quote:<\/div> <table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"> <tr> <td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\">  Originally Posted by <strong>Minde<\/strong> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"><\/span>  <div  style=\"font-style:italic\">Here are all the pictures below...<br \/> <br \/> I used cover paper that you can get at Michaels. I found it a bit cheaper through a wholesale paper company but it is identical to the sparkly stuff they sell at Michaels. Laser printers will not work for metallic like paper! I tried 3! I printed that on a Lexmark 2500 all in one which feeds from the top and comes out the front. This is a must! anything that has to make a sharp turn won't work. I got that printer at Wal-Mart for about $50 I think. <br \/> <br \/> The inside sheets are HP brochure paper. Kinda slick and about 28 lb I think. No see through at all. Those I printed on a color laser printer but an inkjet would have done them too. <br \/> <br \/> I used Word to print the envelopes, again must be on a printer that feeds from the top and comes out the front or you will have marks on the envelope. I stamped the back and used a pretty stamp.<br \/> <br \/> Any other questions please ask. I cannot take credit for all of this as I learned and borrowed from others on here!<br \/> <br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000917.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000918.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000919.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000921.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000922.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000923.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i303.photobucket.com\/albums\/nn123\/mindej\/P1000924.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><\/div> <\/td> <\/tr> <\/table> <\/div><br \/> <br \/> Question: The paper that is on the inside of the Passport - did the blue speck pattern print out as well? Or did you buy paper like that and then print on the paper?\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"info@anaandgordon.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1221648021,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-211786.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"anita","Id":211786,"Name":"anita","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15009,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2393895fddac8d90c0359ac2fd9f41a7","RawContent":"Ok Guys so sorry that I quoted that entire post on my previous entry - I am a noobie and promsie to learn from my mistakes!! &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/pokestick.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Pokestick\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/&gt;\n \n I am going to make up for it by posting these instructions on how to make passport covers yourself that look like the one below (I found it on the DIY Ntwrk). It is a great alternative for trying to make one&#039;s that are thicker than paper. I am going to attempt them and I will post them once I do!\n \n &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/img.diynetwork.com\/DIY\/2006\/01\/26\/dcrj210l_3ca_e.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;span huddler_attributes=\"{&amp;quot;plugin&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;attachment&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;params&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;id&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;5331&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;name&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Passport Cover.ppt&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;description&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;size&amp;quot;:114,&amp;quot;type&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;ppt&amp;quot;}}\" huddler_plugin=\"attachment\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":470662,"PostDate":1223019145,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Ok Guys so sorry that I quoted that entire post on my previous entry - I am a noobie and promsie to learn from my mistakes!! <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/pokestick.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Pokestick\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> I am going to make up for it by posting these instructions on how to make passport covers yourself that look like the one below (I found it on the DIY Ntwrk). It is a great alternative for trying to make one's that are thicker than paper. I am going to attempt them and I will post them once I do!<br \/> <br \/> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/img.diynetwork.com\/DIY\/2006\/01\/26\/dcrj210l_3ca_e.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Click the image to open in full size.\" class=\"tcattdimgresizer\" \/><\/span><p>\u00a0<\/p><span huddler_attributes=\"{\"plugin\":\"attachment\",\"params\":{\"id\":\"5331\",\"name\":\"Passport Cover.ppt\",\"description\":\"\",\"size\":114,\"type\":\"ppt\"}}\" huddler_plugin=\"attachment\">\u00a0<\/span>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"info@anaandgordon.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1221648021,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-211786.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType